The Dark Bramble was three [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]] who broke off from the rest long ago: the Beast, [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]] and [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]]. They meant to hurry the end of the Astra instead of preventing it, which made them enemies of the other Thessians and of all mortal life. The Thessians made a temporary alliance with the greatest mortal military of the time, the Fifth [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Sundom]], and the alliance made war on the Dark Bramble over [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]. It slew the Beast but could not permanently kill the other two, so together they built a jail that could hold the Dark Bramble even if it could not kill them: [[Phenomena/Althane/The Lighthouse|the Lighthouse]], inside a support structure the size of a moon, [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]].

Moments after the Lighthouse was deployed, the Sundom captured the Dark Bramble on Althane and betrayed the alliance, hiding Althane, the Thessian corpses and the Lighthouse from the rest of the Thessians. Althane's own tellings remember only that there was a great fight, that everyone who fought died, and that the world was remade with its memory taken.

The Crystalpoint Lattice came with the Dark Bramble and spent years trying to bring it back to power, reaching out to Thessians it believed were still alive. The quarry who piloted the Lattice were tethered to it, and it was they who woke [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]].
